# =============================================================================
# AR Studio — environment template
# =============================================================================
# Copy to .env.local for local development:   cp .env.example .env.local
# .env.local is gitignored. Never commit real values.
#
# These are the ONLY three variables the application reads. (Verified by grep
# across src/ and scripts/.) If you find DATABASE_URL or NEXTAUTH_* referenced
# in older docs, they are vestigial — nothing reads them.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which project these point at IS the environment. There is no other switch.
# Get values from: Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
#
#   local      -> output of `npx supabase start` (see below)
#   staging    -> ohgqgkraybpvnfdbgmvl   ("AR studio dummy database")
#   production -> drdnqsjjxmqiklwfadmk   ("AR studio") — NEVER in a local file
#
# The refs are not secrets: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is compiled into the
# browser bundle, so both are already public. The keys below are what matter.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are compiled into the browser bundle. They are public
# by design. Do not put anything secret behind that prefix.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER ONLY. Bypasses every RLS policy — this is a full database bypass.
# - Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_
# - Only ever imported from src/app/api/** (CI enforces this)
# - If this leaks, rotate the JWT secret immediately
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Local development
# =============================================================================
# Preferred: run the whole stack locally, touching no hosted project at all.
#
#   npx supabase start
#
# It prints an API URL, anon key, and service_role key. Paste those above.
# The local keys are fixed demo values and are safe to share.
#
#   npx supabase db reset    # replay all migrations from zero
#   npx supabase stop        # shut it down
#
# =============================================================================
# Which environment am I pointed at?
# =============================================================================
#   npm run env:check          # what will the next write touch?
#   npm run env:deploy-check   # what would a build here ship?
#
# Run env:check before anything that writes. The seed scripts run the same
# check and refuse to execute against production.
#
# env:deploy-check also runs automatically as `predev` and `prebuild`, so
# `npm run dev` and `npm run build` both refuse to start against production.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STAGING_PROJECT_REF (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for an ephemeral Supabase *branch* project, which gets a fresh ref
# that cannot be hardcoded. The permanent staging project above is recognised
# without it. Setting this can never unlock production — that check runs first.
# STAGING_PROJECT_REF=
